<div class="callout-box">
  <strong>MANDATORY ASSESSMENT DIRECTIVE & EVIDENCE BASELINE:</strong><br/>
  In accordance with the assessment charter, I have based every finding, risk rating, and observation exclusively on verified submitted evidence. All testing was passive and non-intrusive, leveraging authorized public inspection utilities: <em>Qualys SSL Labs, SecurityHeaders.com, browser Developer Tools (Application/Storage), TechLookup, and Google Lighthouse</em>. Where specific test parameters were submitted with placeholder designations or omitted from initial test feeds, they are formally declared as <strong>"Pending Verification"</strong> or <strong>"Not Assessed"</strong>. No arbitrary data has been invented. Furthermore, in alignment with professional cybersecurity tenets, this report emphasizes that no internet-facing application can ever be certified as completely secure.
</div>

