<h3>6.2 Core Web Vitals & Loading Metrics</h3>
<p>Core Web Vitals represent Google's standardized metrics for measuring real-world user experience and visual stability:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 35%;">Metric Name</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Reported Metric Value</th>
      <th style="width: 40%;">Industry Target Threshold</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>First Contentful Paint (FCP)</strong></td>
      <td><code>[FCP value]</code></td>
      <td>&le; 1.8 seconds (Good)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</strong></td>
      <td><code>[LCP value]</code></td>
      <td>&le; 2.5 seconds (Good)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Total Blocking Time (TBT)</strong></td>
      <td><code>[TBT value]</code></td>
      <td>&le; 200 milliseconds (Good)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)</strong></td>
      <td><code>[CLS value]</code></td>
      <td>&le; 0.1 (Good)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Speed Index (SI)</strong></td>
      <td><code>[Speed Index value]</code></td>
      <td>&le; 3.4 seconds (Good)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>6.3 Issues Identified in Audit Payload</h3>
<p>The test results input documented: <code>[issues found]</code>.</p>
<p>Standard architectural bottlenecks that typically suppress these metrics include uncompressed image assets, unminified script bundles, render-blocking third-party trackers, missing <code>aria-label</code> tags on interactive controls, absence of semantic HTML landmarks, and missing structured data (JSON-LD) required for AI search bots and agentic crawlers.</p>

